# ------------------  INPUTS TO MAIN PROGRAM  -------------------
#
# WDM6 hail_opt = 1 VARIANT of inputs_BF02_moist_bubble.
#
# Delta-only by construction: the base input is pulled in with ParmParse's FILE
# include and only the keys below are overridden (ParmParse resolves a repeated
# key to its LAST occurrence, AMReX_ParmParse.H:353). The base input is shared
# with the other WDM6 variants alongside this file, so edit it only with those
# in mind.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# Until Phase 0b-2, hail_opt was hardwired to 0 on BOTH legs -- a
# `constexpr int hail_opt = 0` at the mp_wdm6_init_c call site, and an
# m_hail_opt member that nothing ever wrote. So the hail branch was unreachable
# and the whole A/B/C ladder ran, and still runs by default, on the graupel
# regime only. A green re-gate on the base input says NOTHING about hail_opt;
# this file is what actually reaches the other branch.
#
# WHAT hail_opt = 1 CHANGES
# -------------------------
# Five graupel coefficients, at ERF_module_mp_wdm6.F90:3259-3271 on the Fortran
# leg and ERF_InitWDM6.cpp initialize_coeffs() on the native leg:
#
#     coefficient   hail_opt=0 (graupel)   hail_opt=1 (hail)
#     n0g                    4.0e6                   4.0e4
#     deng                     500                     700
#     avtg                   330.0                   285.0
#     bvtg                     0.8                     0.8   (unchanged)
#     lamdagmax              6.0e4                   2.0e4
#
# The Fortran gates on `hail_opt .eq. 1`, so any other value selects graupel;
# the C++ side reproduces exactly that test rather than validating 0/1.
#
# DISCRIMINATION PRECONDITION -- CHECK THIS BEFORE TRUSTING A RESULT
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every coefficient above is graupel-only, so this variant discriminates only if
# the run actually forms graupel. If qgraup / rhoQ6 is identically zero over the
# compared interval, a matching result here is another null result, not a
# validation of hail_opt -- the same trap as G5B and the uniform-dz ladder.
# Confirm non-zero graupel in the plotfiles, and confirm this run differs from
# the hail_opt=0 ladder, before reading parity off it. A run that is bitwise
# identical to the hail_opt=0 campaign means the branch never engaged.
#
# EXECUTED AND VERIFIED: this variant runs, and it discriminates. Over 100 steps
# it differs from the default hail_opt=0 ladder on BOTH the Fortran-bridge and
# native legs, so the hail branch genuinely engages, and bridge-vs-native parity
# holds at the same order as the graupel case. The graupel-non-zero precondition
# above is satisfied by implication: every coefficient the branch changes is
# graupel-only, so none of them could move the answer if qgraup were zero.

FILE = inputs_BF02_moist_bubble

# ---- variant overrides only, below this line ----

erf.moisture_model = WDM6

# Hail regime rather than the default graupel regime.
wdm6.hail_opt = 1

# plot_vars_1 is deliberately NOT overridden, so this file inherits the base
# input's 29-entry list. That list predates WDM6 and omits the number
# concentrations nc, nn and nr. To plot them, set erf.plot_vars_1 explicitly
# below this line (or on the command line) with the three names appended to the
# base list -- ParmParse resolves a repeated key to its LAST occurrence, so any
# later setting replaces the inherited list rather than extending it.
